<title>INDIA: India's BASF 1996/97 net lower.</title>
<headline>India's BASF 1996/97 net lower.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>year to March 31, 1997.</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit	    161.72     vs     200.91</p>
<p>    Income		2,710.15     vs   2,439.67</p>
<p>    Div (in rupees)	 3.00     vs	 --</p>
<p>    Gross profit	  504.14     vs     382.89</p>
<p>    Interest		218.50     vs     106.24</p>
<p>    Depreciation	  132.92     vs	52.74</p>
<p>    Tax			20.20     vs	23.0</p>
<p>Note: BASF India is the subsidiary of the German chemical giant, BASF AG. BASF India said 1996/97 export sales were 168.02 million rupees against 189.87 million in the previous year.</p>
<p>The firm said it will hold its annual general meeting on August 8.</p>
<p>-- Bombay equities +91-22-265 9000</p>
